    "content": "NATO stands for the North Atlantic Treaty Organization, a political and military alliance established in 1949 to guarantee the freedom and security of its members through collective defense. Based in Brussels, it acts as a mutual defense pact, where an attack on one member is considered an attack against all. It currently has 32 member countries. Key aspects of NATO include: Purpose: Created to provide collective security against the Soviet Union initially, its focus is now maintaining peace and defending against modern threats. Article 5: This core tenet states that if a NATO ally is a victim of an armed attack, all other members will consider this act of violence as an armed attack against all members and will take actions to assist, including the use of armed force. Membership: Comprised of 32 countries from Europe and North America, including the United States, Canada, the UK, France, and Germany. Decision-Making: Decisions are made by consensus, meaning all members must agree. Name in French: Often called Organisation du traité de l'Atlantique nord (OTAN).",
